    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "This thesis project explores the art of Charlotte Salomon, who created a gesamtkunstwerk entitled “Life? or Theatre?” — chronicling her life story — in the midst of WWII, while hiding in exile from the Nazis. Applying the philosophies of Nietzsche and Kierkegaard, this thesis argues that Salomon’s project was an artistic leap of faith, evidencing her belief in life despite the darkness that surrounded her. It explores the redemptive aspects of art amidst great loss, and how this artistic redemption differs from notions of Judeo-Christian redemption. Finally, the thesis talks about what it means to be a receiver of a work of art, analogizing the experience to that of the serendipity of receiving a message in a bottle from the sea.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
